# Branded receipt/refund email links and logo; canonical HTTPS origin, no trailing slash.
skopia.mail.public-origin=${SKOPIA_MAIL_PUBLIC_ORIGIN:https://skopia.randillasith.me}

# Password reset backend configuration
# Set a canonical HTTPS origin for links (no path, query, fragment or trailing slash).
skopia.password-reset.public-origin=${SKOPIA_PASSWORD_RESET_PUBLIC_ORIGIN:https://skopia.randillasith.me}
# Reset mail reuses skopia.mail.enabled, skopia.mail.from and the existing
# authenticated STARTTLS skopia.mail.host/port/username/password sender.
# If mail or the origin is misconfigured, every address receives the same 503; no token is issued.
# Accepted requests remain generic because async SMTP failure cannot be reported to the requester.
# Watch for PASSWORD_RESET_DELIVERY_FAILED and password-reset delivery queue warnings.
